  message: "Merged in PR #2253. Close condition, point by point.\nENUMERATION (kept in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/state/; now also the guard itself, hypergumbo_core/kept_work_guard.py): 112 state-write sites in 84 functions across packages/*/src, packages/*/tests and tests: global 31, mutate 58, lazy self-attribute 23 (no cached_property). WHAT THE SCAN CANNOT SEE (the guard's docstring): state reached through an alias or a container passed in, a module's state written from another module, class-level containers changed through cls/self, setattr/globals() writes, lazy attributes on an object other than self, lambda bodies, C extensions; scripts/ is not read.\nSHAPE 1, hand-written caches: MECHANISM hypergumbo_core.kept_work (used on every call, filling around the work), which the recorder treats as a cached function's call and body. 22 functions marked (18 caches, 4 warn-once flags). Census first (state/census_summary.txt): a context around every call would cost 209 s of worker time; marking the fill costs 21,926 labelled fills + 280,050 uses = about 12 s of worker time, about 2 s wall on 6 workers (state/kw/, full run 2). LIVE CONTROLS (state/control/), each a full run with the fault, out of the index: framework aliases dropped in _read_framework_patterns: 7 failed, 6 selected, 1 named as coverage cannot speak for (test_route_concept_parity.py::test_route_detected[rust]), 0 neither; short-name index dropped in _read_function_summaries: 4 failed, 4 selected, 0 neither (585 of 609 reaching tests could be left out). MUTATIONS (state/mutations.tsv): 30 planted in kept_work, the recorder's hook and the guard, 30 red.\nSHAPE 2, lazy state on an object a shared fixture returns: every lazy self-attribute the scan found (23 sites) is on an object made per analysis run or filled at construction (EXEMPT gives each reason; spot-checked by reading ada, rust, scala, verilog, circom, bitbake, LinkerContext, _NameTable). None was found on an object a shared fixture returns, so no function needed a mechanism; the guard makes every new such method be marked or exempted with a reason. NOT asserted: lazy state the scan cannot see (an attribute on an object other than self, e.g. the registry index holder's builders, which ARE marked by hand).\nGUARD: scripts/check-kept-work and test_kept_work_guard.py::test_live_tree_is_clean fail on a state-writing function neither marked nor exempted (62 exemptions with reasons), on a marked fill with no use, on an exemption marked too, and on a stale exemption. It runs in every full run (the scheduled suite included) and when the guard's modules change, NOT on every PR; wiring it into pre-commit touches .githooks (governance) and is a question for the owner.\nFULL RUNS: 41,381 passed (721 s). Fold: 66 fixture + 41 cache contexts (22 before). Never narrowed 447 (428 before): tests that only hit the VCS-ignore answer now inherit the git its fill ran. One earlier full run had 2 order-dependent failures, filed separately."  # d13e
